lue":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T08:06:06-07:00","id":126710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=126545#post126545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can ask, though it was not cut because it was the awesomest stuff that ever awesomed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm comfortable with you posting the cut part of your draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T11:14:33-07:00","id":126818,"title":"","content":"Hey Baron. Thanks for dropping by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=126501#post126501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to not make it look like there was a pogrom on AA. It's more a matter of Sin-Eaters are wary of them, and word on the street/web is they are bad news. A Storyteller is welcome to take that in a dire direction, but AA is not going the way of the dodo anytime soon...well, not due to Sin-Eaters, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be pleased to know that came through in the text.<br /> <br /> It wasn't that I got the impression that there is a pogrom, it's that I got the impression there will be sometime soon. This bit for example: The situation is tense, and it\u2019s leading up to a great conflict.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:48:37-07:00","id":128531,"title":"","content":"<b>The Cycle Turns</b><br /> <br /> The opening section for the Arisen focuses less on theme and more on giving details on what the mummies are. This is presentable, but in my opinion a bit less useful than moods and themes. Even if you assume that the players haven't read Mummy: the Curse, the Mummy's goal is actually mostly irrelevant. The unstoppable nearly unthinking automaton as an enemy works if it's trying to steal that artefact, or kill someone who said something rude in front of Tutenkahmen's tomb.<br /> <br /> The bit about how fighting Mummies is bad for the duped cultists in the crossfire was good, and made me realise how much the hunting Vampires section could benefit from that; as well as the possibility to fight Mummies/Vampires with buy outs and stock holder rebellions that's less harmful to the little guy. The Barrett Commission kinda rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Response:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey -</b> The section on the response opens by saying Mumies are the Unknown and the Unkowable; then Ashwood Abbey gives nothing on the Abbey's views on mummies, how they interact with them. It gives one specific Abbey clubhouse having trouble with one specific mummy.<br /> <br /> You know, I think I like it. Wordcount-stuff-I've-said-before. Another two examples showing different angles would have been good.<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night \u2013</b> The same here, a slightly longer section (fitting Mummy's and The Long Night's shared themes of religion). Here we have a Mummy poaching worshippers from a Long Night Church who are gearing up to fight back. It seems this Mummy is racist too. A nice way to tie the Mummy's old fashioned ideas into the story, but I wasn't keen on how it downplayed the religious themes to focus on the racial. Some examples of how a Mummy cult atract Christian's with it's own scripture would be very useful.<br /> <br /> <b>The Loyalists of Thule \u2013</b> This section really goes on about the Ageis Kai Doru doesn't it? I felt there was a bit too much filler here. In fact I could summarise it in a couple of sentences \u201cThe Loyalists of Thule have been tracking artefacts moving through New York Harbour and intercepting the really dangerous ones. The a Rabbi with a mysterious debt to a Mummy promises he can destroy any artefact.\u201d It's a good plot hook, but with word count so tight I really felt the filler.<br /> <br /> I'm going to summarise the rest of the Compacts here because I have the same thing to say about all of them.<br /> <br /> I've fallen out of love with the idea. These aren't Compact write ups, they're story hooks. In fact they're good story hooks \u2013 well The Union's one was pretty basic \u2013 but they don't give you any idea about how a Compact will react. There's no \u201cStoryteller's guide\u201d or \u201cplayer's guide\u201d.<br /> <br /> Now I know the core theme is that they don't know about Mummies (and credit where it's due, it's actually nice to see a section stick with it's theme), but that doesn't matter. There's plenty you can talk about without requiring that knowledge. What do they think about people destroying artefacts, about cults, about mystical architecture. Or how do they feel about being hutned down by an unstoppable foe with tons of minions. Pick something they're likely to notice before they learn the word \u201cMummy\u201d and you've got your *'s guide.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Agis Kai Doru \u2013</b> Fans have been talking about AKD/Mummies probably since before Mummy was published. So with a lot riding on this one I'm pleased to say it did not disappoint. This is, in my opinion, how Conspiracies should have been portrayed since day one.<br /> <br /> It talks about the AKD as a large international organisation, with: internal politics (Encounters with Mummies stain you for life, no one wants to give you Relics that the Mummy will take when it eventually kills you)<br /> <br /> Lots of lore: They basically know the useful stuff about mummy nature, useful as in useful for fighting them.<br /> <br /> Money, manpower and top down strategy to use them: Their basic plan is to send in the Sword to avoid yet district the Mummy by fighting it's cult, while the Temple sneak in, nab the relics, and get them to Athens where the Mummy probably can't track it.<br /> <br /> Membership is sinister: The Sword are practically disposable cannon fodder used as a distraction.<br /> <br /> There was something I felt was missing though, a sidebar addressing the big question. Why are the AKD not tied to Mummies instead of Vampires/Werewolves? I think replacing the fiction (a letter between two Guardians) with options for alternative Guardian back-stories would be a massive improvement. (e.g. A former mummy cult that forgot they ever were a mummy cult. The special forces of an opressed Nameless Empire colony that started stealing Relics and fighting back after Irem fell and just kept going when their country ceased to exist. The whole Conspiracy is an sham, it's members are really getting Relics so it's secret masters can use them to repeat the Rite of Return and become Gods like they believe happened in Irem) <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones -</b> Despite the Egypt connection there isn't much wordcount spent here, but I like it. They defeated the Mummies back in Egypt and are slowly learning that this is not the case, and preparing for war.<br /> <br /> It's a good angle, but how on Earth did they miss the last Sothic Cycle? They're 1,461 years long, so they'd have been at least one between now and ancient Egypt. Still, it feels like Conspiracy stuff. Ancient secrets and international organisations slowly building up steam.<br /> <br /> <b>Cherion Group \u2013 </b>We're back to sort of plot-hooks again. Two of them, one suggests they're attempting to acquire Last Dynasty International without ever mentioning the name, I approve. The other suggests they brought out a cult's front company and are now having a bit of trouble getting what they want from it.<br /> <br /> It feels like conspiracy stuff again, but while I forgive the Ascending One's for not giving much players guide stuff due to word count, here I feel it's lack a little stronger. There's good stuff between the lines, but it's between the lines.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge \u2013</b> And now more player's guide / storytellers guide. This one didn't feel quite so Conspiracyish, but that's ok. The Lucifuge is closer to a Compact anyway. I didn't like the bit that cults are either demonic or Mummy; Vampires and Fae both start cults in their line, you can separate out Infernal and Unchained demons, then you get to old gods like Odin, or completely mortal cult leaders.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum \u2013</b> Catholic theology is pretty clear that everything supernatural is demonic or heavenly. The whole section can be summarised as \u201ctheologically troubling\u201d, but Mummies really are not. To the MM they'd probably be just a form of demon, or perhaps someone sold their soul for immortality; the fact that Mummies didn't get real immortality would have solid scriptural backing, only god can grant true eternal life so when you sell your soul to the devil for eternal life you end up a shambling mummy like thing. Also, nothing at all on the fact we're talking about a rival religion?<br /> <br /> <b>TF:V \u2013</b> they don't know about Mummies, but are pretty good at handling the mortal side of cults. That seems fitting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Habiti Ma \u2013 </b>A modern day Egyptian group using the name of an old Egyptian god. I have no idea how plausible that is, or if it's supposed to be a difference between the WoD and our world. After all, in the WoD Ma'at is probably a real goddess who might want to spread her name a little. Also, I think this is the first (official) Vigil org with no presence in the USA (not counting that one in the Vampire book). About time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cult deprogrammers is a yet unfilled niche in Vigil, and I'm pleased to see it being handled well. The Enemy section also suggests that Ma'at might actually be involved in this, but it's an extremely vague possibility with many other options.<br /> <br /> The very subtle reference / insult against Taken made me laugh.<br /> <br /> I was a little disappointed that the Duties didn't give free specificities like they do in Compacts and Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The Status dots give you Mystery Cult Initiation? Ok, I presume that means you've infiltrated a Cult, but it doesn't say that. It's also a little weird that the 5 dot status people are infiltrating, 5 dots should mostly be desk jobs.<br /> <br /> The Ascending Ones stereotype reads like the Ascending Ones talking about Habiti Ma, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Faithful of Shulpae \u2013</b> So six years after The Marduk Society (Leviathan: the Tempest) Hunter introduces a second group dedicated to eating monsters for immortality. Not that it matters, since for Marduk it's mostly backstory, here it's the main course (pun intended).<br /> <br /> I like the concept. There's nothing wrong with a Hunter trying to kill monsters, but I do like verity and these guy certainly add a little spice (pun intended).<br /> <br /> The section on The Enemy lists \u201cPromethians, werewolves and vampires\u201d. Seriously? No Mermaids. Mermaids actually have mythology about being eaten for immortality. (BTW, Werewolves don't have much longivity)<br /> <br /> The picture \u2013 utterly utterly brilliant.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure if these guys are a Compact or a Conspiracy, I'm leaning towards Compact since I don't think they have that much in the way of numbers or organisation.<br /> <br /> I don't really have much to say other than I like them, and can the next group trying to gain magic powers be less evil please.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Story Hooks \u2013</b> These two I wasn't a big fan of, they seemed straight forward and thus didn't grab me.<br /> <br /> Wondering Monsters \u2013 We only get one Mummy, and not a very good one. The problems are two fold, firstly there's no cult. I don't think you can have a Mummy without a cult, literally, don't Mummies radiate a \u201ccult creation aura\u201d while they're asleep. Even if you could, this is the example Mummy so rare oddities like not having a Cult shouldn't be included.<br /> <br /> Secondly is the use of modern gender ideas. Mummies are quite strongly defined by having an identity that's broadly speaking, bronze age. It's entirely possible that a Mummy would be genderless, but it not look anything like modern ideas of genderlessness. I do find it ironic that in a book with chapters for Promethian, Changeling, Geist and Demon \u2013 all games which strongly support characters exploring their gender identity, it showed up in the one game where it doesn't fit (at least in a recognisably modern form).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Conclusions \u2013</b> This chapter was one of extremes. What it did right it typically did very right. The Agis Kai Doru was brilliant and most of the other Conspiracies were at least very good. The new organisations were both done very well.<br /> <br /> The Compacts on the other hand, I ended up not feeling the idea of portraying them entirely as Storyhooks. I would rather have seen advice on where they'd likely go after they learned about Mummies, or what they'd think about Mummy cults in general written from the perspective that they don't know about the Mummies at the heart. The Malleus pinned itself entirely on a theological issue that under catholic scripture, really should not be an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:28:42-07:00","id":128559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven;n128531<br /> <br /> [B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malleus Maleficarum \u2013[/B] Catholic theology is pretty clear that everything supernatural is demonic or heavenly. The whole section can be summarised as \u201ctheologically troubling\u201d, but Mummies really are not. To the MM they'd probably be just a form of demon, or perhaps someone sold their soul for immortality; the fact that Mummies didn't get real immortality would have solid scriptural backing, only god can grant true eternal life so when you sell your soul to the devil for eternal life you end up a shambling mummy like thing. Also, nothing at all on the fact we're talking about a rival religion?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The pharaoh of Egypt have their magics, true. But see how long they endured. Frightfully powerful at first but until they again crumple into dust. An eternal ozymandias. Doomed to watch their efforts fall again and again. They offer no gifts of healing nor careful balm to their followers. They have no empathy for those below them nor do they even hide that fact. As such, their kingdom is all too mortal and temporary, forever doomed to repeat a cycle that is never ending. Take heed brothers and sisters, for there is a lesson here that the Lord is teaching us! Our Lord gives us calm in the storm of our lives. Allows for mercy while others cry for death. Other demand their servants toil and die for their own pleasure, no hope of knowing the amazing grace that we so take for granted. For though we may age and die, the kingdom of our Lord is everlasting and in his kingdom, no one shall remain a slave!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":".  edit: threw in some extra words to make it sound better. 05-09-2014, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:30:36-07:00","id":128562,"title":"","content":"Amen.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">+charlimit</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:51:04-07:00","id":128582,"title":"","content":"Back somewhat to my point:<br /> <br /> The MM doesn't dispute the fact that there maybe other players that use magic such as the Fae or the Egyptians (Moses had to face off with Egyptian priests, The MM knows about the Fae, and less we forget Peter's dealing with Simon) but focus on the meaning behind it. So what if the spell works? Are you using it for your own personal power? What happens to the people lower than you? How do your ethos treat them? <br /> <br /> One of the reasons why I think that religions became the way they are (baring Archmages meddling) is they offered something that is more lasting than someone just throwing spells can provide. They offered ethos instead of supernatural side shows and hence why they, not cults worshiping various real life supernatural entities, became so well known today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:59:46-07:00","id":128587,"title":"","content":"I agree fully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=128582#post128582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and less we forget Peter's dealing with Simon</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T16:04:53-07:00","id":128593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=128587#post128587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree fully.<br /> <br /> Wait what?</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>Acts 8:9-24</b><br /><br /> New International Version (NIV)<br /> <br /> <b>Simon the Sorcerer</b><br /><br /> <sup>9 </sup>Now for some time a man named Simon had practiced sorcery in the city and amazed all the people of Samaria. He boasted that he was someone great, <sup>10 </sup>and all the people, both high and low, gave him their attention and exclaimed, \u201cThis man is rightly called the Great Power of God.\u201d <sup>11 </sup>They followed him because he had amazed them for a long time with his sorcery. <sup>12 </sup>But when they believed Philip as he proclaimed the good news of the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women. <sup>13 </sup>Simon himself believed and was baptized. And he followed Philip everywhere, astonished by the great signs and miracles he saw.<br /> <sup>14 </sup>When the apostles in Jerusalem heard that Samaria had accepted the word of God, they sent Peter and John to Samaria. <sup>15 </sup>When they arrived, they prayed for the new believers there that they might receive the Holy Spirit, <sup>16 </sup>because the Holy Spirit had not yet come on any of them; they had simply been baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus. <sup>17 </sup>Then Peter and John placed their hands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit.<br /> <sup>18 </sup>When Simon saw that the Spirit was given at the laying on of the apostles\u2019 hands, he offered them money <sup>19 </sup>and said, \u201cGive me also this ability so that everyone on whom I lay my hands may receive the Holy Spirit.\u201d<br /> <sup>20 </sup>Peter answered: \u201cMay your money perish with you, because you thought you could buy the gift of God with money! <sup>21 </sup>You have no part or share in this ministry, because your heart is not right before God. <sup>22 </sup>Repent of this wickedness and pray to the Lord in the hope that he may forgive you for having such a thought in your heart. <sup>23 </sup>For I see that you are full of bitterness and captive to sin.\u201d<br /> <sup>24 </sup>Then Simon answered, \u201cPray to the Lord for me so that nothing you have said may happen to me.\u201d<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T16:10:28-07:00","id":128603,"title":"","content":"Oh, I misread your last point. I read it as you saying Simon was linked to the MM's understanding of the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T16:15:36-07:00","id":128606,"title":"","content":"On an unrelated note, God I hate NIV version. I like me my older syntax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T14:13:27-07:00","id":130160,"title":"","content":"So I didn't finish the demon chapter today. So here's the first bit with more to come soon.<br /> <br /> <b>To Hell and Back</b><br /> <br /> Very first few paragraphs and I am immediately hit by a feeling of \u201cthis is about Unchained\u201d! No problem, but it's worth mentioning. We'll see what happens when we get to the Lucifuge though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then we get to lesser demons. Bodyless, tied to Vice, using words from Inferno. But a mouth full of grinding gears? Is the intent to blur the lines between Inferno and Unchained, hinting at an upcomming expansion to Unchained or just that Infernal demons can be asthetically mechanical too? I'm just hoping there's a clear statement of what's what later.<br /> <br /> The lesser demons section continues this blurring, lots of Unchained imagery but creatures that would fit right at home in Inferno and look a bit out of place in Unchained. The greater demons, however, are clearly unchained. Also, Lucifer is a signal. Yay! Though I'm only dimly aware of that idea moving around the forums I did like the concept. <br /> <br /> Pacts are good. The concept that demonic pacts do take some of your soul is new to Unchained (as far as I know) and deserves more material. You can't just say souls are being trimmed and not mention it again, though saying it grows back would be enough. All in all, I liked the pact section, I dind't quite feel the mortal pactee's motivation but it's just an example.<br /> <br /> Purposes \u2013 it seemed ok, but I've already read the Agendas so I mostly skipped over this. Same with the power section just afterwords.<br /> <br /> Institutional Demons \u2013 once again I get the feeling that these guys are Inferno. The G-M and the Unchained cannot be so easily pegged as \u201calways making the world worse\u201d. In fact, I really hope this is inferno because I think it would be a big blow for Demon's themes if the G-M's actions were so concretely defined. Even the Fiendish Flaws feel a little more occult and less technical than usual. Notice that nothing mentions silicon or circuitry.<br /> <br /> Witnesses: Nice and simple, though these obviously Stigmatics come from all types of demons, further confusing the question: Unchained or Infernal.<br /> <br /> So, my thoughts. It was functional, but like most of the opening sections it's mostly for people who haven't read Demon. I have, well the kickstarter preview anyway. I think a small sidebar addressing what's Unchained or what's Inferno was really really needed. My final guess is, this is all Unchained but it's really non obvious and could have been easily cleared up. I kinda hope I'm wrong though, the portrayal of Lesser and Institutional demons, I don't think it works for Unchained.<br /> <br /> Having ready all the opening sections; I give the award to Jason Needham. I think his decision to focus less on mechanics and factual info, and more on presenting the themes worked great. In general I think mechanics are easy, themes are hard, so that's a better place to focus. Plus it's useful if you have or haven't read Geist, and heck it's even useful reading if you're playing Geist without Hunters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T15:26:14-07:00","id":130402,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, hunters would also have some serious problems with determining a difference between Descent and Inferno demons, even if they knew the lingo. A great many of them don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T00:46:15-07:00","id":131761,"title":"","content":"That still doesn't mean that the reader should have trouble telling them apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I'm not too sure if it really would be that hard. Some broad steryotypes that are 80% accurate and easy to check. If it's pacts require you to do stuff or make sacrifices: Inferno. If it wants pieces of your history: Unchained. If it's an ephemeral being: Inferno. If it's physical: Unchained. If he's harmed by a blessed item: Possessed. If not: Stigmatic.<br /> <br /> A demon may intentionally disgusie itself as the other kind; but if they don't do that it should be quite easy to tell them apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T02:11:54-07:00","id":131941,"title":"","content":"I'm really suprised that they didn't add more with TF:V.<br /> <br /> TF:V having super advanced tech? It's primary mission most notably being the ones that make sure that supernatural crap doesn't hit the fan or some supernaturals make the next 9-11? A black budget that seems to conjure cash out of nowhere. The entire organization being built on the premise of intelligence work and the like.<br /> <br /> I would personally be surprised if there wasn't an angel pulling the strings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T08:45:44-07:00","id":132310,"title":"","content":"The Response<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey</b> \u2013 The Ashwood Abbey is split into the three subgroups. The Competitors enjoy unravelling a demon's webs of lies to track it down. The Pursuit are fascinated by the theological mysteries. Libertienes like to get possessed for fun.<br /> <br /> Libertines were exactly what I expected. The other two, not so much. I always saw good ol' Abbey as being about quick cheap thrills, while the Competitors seem to be playing the long game which I can certainly see being a niche hobby, anticipation has it's own sort of thrill. The Pursuit are more interested in awful taboo breaking secrets rather than knowledge itself. I don't see them as interested in the truths of the universe, so much as which celebrity sold her soul to who.<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night</b> \u2013 We come to our first religious hunters in the demons chapter. This section has about half a paragraph on the Long Night's views, tactics, lore, etc. The rest is from the demon's point of view, why might a demon target a church community? Considering this is repeating stuff that was mentioned a few pages ago, I didn't like this section.<br /> <br /> Even if you talk exclusively about the Unchained \u2013 who have no religious connection to the Long Night \u2013 there's a whole wealth of interesting parallels. Does a person accept suffering and hardship on Earth in faith that he'll be rewarded in heaven, or take the easy way out and sign on the dotted line? That's the core of Christian theology, and it applies just as well to Unchained as Inferno. At least the Long Night will assume it does, because they'll assume an Unchained contract's are damming. There's lots of missed potential here.<br /> <br /> The Loyalists of Thule \u2013 this one is very straight forward. Sometimes they collaborate with demons for information, when they don't they are very good at sniffing out the discrepancies in cover. I did like the idea that the Loyalists would intentionally turn their lives into a minefield if it looks like a demon wants to buy it. If you think you're doomed to hell, maybe oblivion would be better.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero</b> \u2013 another straight forward one. They will get a demon transforming on camera one day and then what? Each group's opinion is presented.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis</b> \u2013 The Rationalists know about lessoer demons, but haven't had much luck getting them to hold still enough to study. Still, they accept their existence which is always good. Greater Demons seem to have hidden from them so far. Open Minds have laxer standards, and the cataclysmics suspect a war they know nothing about is coming. Sadly, nothing was done with the idea that Embeds are laws of physics, and interesting things could happen if the NM found them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Union</b> \u2013 demons being particularly infrastructural makes the union think about three letter agencies, banks, and soon they're moving from Home Front to General Strike. It's a good angle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ageis Kai Doru </b>\u2013 This entire section is one big plot hook. Behind the scenes I believe what happened was that some ancient Greeks tried to build an epic bit of Infrastructure, the AKD stopped them leaving the device sunk on the ocean floor. Now in the 20th century they've finally managed to start carefully gathering pieces and trying to figure out what it was.<br /> <br /> There's virtually nothing on their opinions or strategies, but at least it's a good plot hook. The AKD being the second oldest Conspiracy (with more infrastructure to retain the benefits of age than the AO) is, IMO, one of their strongest themes so it's nice to see it played to. I didn't like the fact they never found any other Infrastructure in two thousand years.<br /> <br /> <b>Relic</b> \u2013 long backstory aside, this is a compass that points to demons.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ascending Ones </b>\u2013 As always they don't agree on much. The Southern Temple questions whether demons are the actual demons \u2013 in a way that strongly implies they're not the ones from Inferno. I did like the way they believed in the idea of king Solomon commanding demons. The Knife thinks that demons are bad news, no matter where they come from. The Crescent have on the ground knowledge, and for some reason that's not made clear they aren't sure if the other Ascending Ones are the people they can turn to.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cherion Group </b>\u2013 is Deeva Corporation supposed to be bigher than Cherion? Or just equal so that they can laugh at Cherion thinking they're tiny? Either way, Cherion has a rival for hunting demons, which is unsuprising. I did especially like the way Cherion is behind The Prisoner \u2013 their basic goal is to learn how to make Demons into their apocalyptic forms so that they can be harvested.<br /> <br /> Cheiron gets no Endowment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge</b> \u2013 This one... it's not very good. Lets start with the preliminaries. The Lucifuge are descended from Inferno, not Unchained. Castigation is solid evidence for this. Pre GMC you got bonuses for low morality. The Familiar Castigation is damn near identical to the one in Inferno. Actually, it's explicitly said so. Les Infants Diabolic and Lucifuge are said to be targeting the same people for Recruitment, Inferno page 180.<br /> <br /> So the starting point is that Lucifuge are tied to inferno. Now Inferno has a whole demonic theology, and a brief mention of an angelic counterpart (p 158). So you'd expect there to be some interesting theological debates; about how these two gods with their angels and their fallen angels fit together into a broader universe.<br /> <br /> Well, nope. The whole section can be summeriesd as \u201cIf a Lucifuge is convinced that the Unchained view is the core cosmology, here's how they might react\u201d. I would describe it as guidelines for how to make Lucifuge fit into the Unchained setting, but this is a Hunter book, the Lucifgue's own worldview and cosmology deserves more weight than this. There is room for a Lucifuge who comes to believe that we're all living in the God Machine's personal universe, and all the other angels and demons are creations of rival gods poking their heads in. But not at the expense of the Lucifuge's own world-view.<br /> <br /> <b>The Malleus Maleficarum</b> - This one on the other hand is quite nice. It says the MM mostly ignore the questions of what's a demon, which Catholic theology would do. Them being influenced by papal policy, and using influence as well as guns. I like that quite a bit. The only missing piece was something on angels.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force VALKARIE</b> \u2013 this one was a bit general. It does seem to imply TF:V are ok with the G-M, but it's probably a bit closer to them not knowing about it and knowing about demons. Demons say it created the world and it's bad. TF:V says the world is pretty ok, so if it created it then it can't be that bad. They might change their mind if they met it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now </b>\u2013 So another corporation trying to harvest the supernatural? This niche is getting quite crowded. I won't say it's over-filled yet, but it will be quite soon.<br /> <br /> First page: They're techno-utopian captalistis. That is a weird mix. Really weird actually. Take this quote from the stereotypes \u201cWe want a future where everyone works for honest dollars\u201d and now this quote from earlier \u201cHis utopia will be founded on principles of self-governance and self-sufficiency. The individual modules of his floating environment will be able to produce goods for<br /> themselves with 3-D printing and other cutting-edge advances.\u201d<br /> <br /> If everyone is self sufficient, what exactly will people be doing for those honest dollars? There's only so many jobs to go around in resource extraction, and designing things to 3-d print will probably end up competing with an open-model community.<br /> <br /> I don't actually think this is a bad concept, though I'm not sure. Utopian visionary with a major blind spot can lead to epic stories. But I would have liked a bit more on the ideological conflict between capitalistic techno-utopians and regular techno-utopians.<br /> <br /> On the whole though, they're a regular hunter group. There's not much methodological distinctions when it comes down to what they do on the ground. They like humanity, dislike monsters, fight like any other hunter group, and specialise in infrastructural demons. A solid compact, but the real story possibilities is where they might go in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Knights of Saint Adrian</b> \u2013 What can I say about these guys that hasn't been said on these forums already?<br /> <br /> I have a strong dislike of hunters who're unwittingly serving monsters. Let me clarify, I'm fine with hunters unwittingly serving monsters appearing as antagonists, but not as the default PCs. Hunter is thematically about playing humans fighting back after all. So these guys, well it's mostly speaking not unwitting.<br /> <br /> They know who they're working for. They're doing it for a pay check. Some might be upset if they learned that \u201cgod\u201d isn't the good guy; but I think at least 60% will just shrug and maybe raise their prices a bit.<br /> <br /> The core concept here is a mixture of Dog the Bounty Hunter and 80s action heroes. It pushes the feel of hunter as a gritty dark game as far as it can go without actually breaking it, and behind the explosions and shiny motorcycles there is a strong element of back room deals and shady characters. All in all, as someone who said that playing a mixed Conspiracy group is almost as much of crossover as playing a Vampires and Changelings; I approve of this new thematic ground.<br /> <br /> Their Endowments are solid, it could use one that boosts Stamina or provides armour. But why does the picture have a guy with no tats?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not going to do a where I read on the entire list of new Mechanics. Except to say Elixirs don't cost exp. About damn time! The new rules for Monsters Don't Count, however, are perhaps the worst possible mechanical decision you could make. [edit - someone on RPG.net suggested that this might refer exclusively to the rule of the same name on page 322 of the Hunter core, if true that would nullify my complaints.]<br /> <br /> There is definitely room in Hunter for paranoid wrecks, but there is also room for stone cold badasses who keep everything together during a long campaign of doing bad things to bad people \u2013 not least because most of the named Hunter NPCs come across as having high Integrity. Does Lady Lucifuge come across as someone who can't hold herself together? How many people has she had tortured or killed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-12-2014, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T09:41:03-07:00","id":132339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=131761#post131761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still doesn't mean that the reader should have trouble telling them apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I'm not too sure if it really would be that hard. Some broad steryotypes that are 80% accurate and easy to check. If it's pacts require you to do stuff or make sacrifices: Inferno. If it wants pieces of your history: Unchained. If it's an ephemeral being: Inferno. If it's physical: Unchained. If he's harmed by a blessed item: Possessed. If not: Stigmatic.<br /> <br /> A demon may intentionally disgusie itself as the other kind; but if they don't do that it should be quite easy to tell them apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>My takeaway was that the whole chapter is about servants of the God-Machine. Imps (Imperatives) and other lesser demons are rogue elements of the God-Machine that aren't human enough for a Cover identity. Like Angels, they are ephemeral. None of this chapter is about Inferno demons. <br /> <br /> Personally, I hope that Heirs to Hell follows up on the story about the Lucifuge's possible origin, even if it ends up contradicting Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T09:42:05-07:00","id":132340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=131761#post131761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still doesn't mean that the reader should have trouble telling them apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I'm not too sure if it really would be that hard. Some broad steryotypes that are 80% accurate and easy to check. If it's pacts require you to do stuff or make sacrifices: Inferno. If it wants pieces of your history: Unchained. If it's an ephemeral being: Inferno. If it's physical: Unchained. If he's harmed by a blessed item: Possessed. If not: Stigmatic.<br /> <br /> A demon may intentionally disgusie itself as the other kind; but if they don't do that it should be quite easy to tell them apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. No. That's not the point at all.<br /> <br /> If I have an objection to Mortal Remains, it really is the departure from earlier books about it being from the hunter's perspective.* The reader should have <i>some</i> trouble telling them apart, because they are getting the experience of the characters they'll be playing. A big point of the supplements, in my opinion, was to help divorce players from their vast store of lore. It doesn't have to work hard for it, and pointing at stuff from the lines is fine, but the books are there to make things occult again.<br /> <br /> I get and appreciate the reason why some of them, like Black Hat Matt, decided not to go that route. But the point isn't just to familiarize people who don't know the lines with them enough for Hunter, it's to defamiliariaze people who do know about them. Hunter is very much about clouded perspectives.<br /> <br /> Reading the Demon chapter was hard for me, because I was trying to translate things into Inferno and Descent, but in all honesty I shouldn't have been doing that, and if I'm honest with myself, I enjoyed reading that chapter(alongside Ghostwalkers and The Undying Ones, despite some of their own issues) more than I did the Promethean or even the Changeling chapter <i>becuase</i> stuff was obfuscated a little bit-familiar enough for me to have ideas, obscure for me to not be sure.<br /> <br /> Mystery is kind of the point.<br /> <br /> EDITTED IN PS: By the way, one of the cool things about the Lucifuge is that their lineages are all fucked up-it's actually harder to tell who their parents are than you'd think. Inferno demons claim a large portion of it, but things like Fae-blooded folks also have room in there, and <i>certainly </i> children of the Unchained have room in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-11-2014, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:01:51-07:00","id":132356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=132340#post132340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDITTED IN PS: By the way, one of the cool things about the Lucifuge is that their lineages are all fucked up-it's actually harder to tell who their parents are than you'd think. Inferno demons claim a large portion of it, but things like Fae-blooded folks also have room in there, and <i>certainly </i> children of the Unchained have room in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my personal canon that the Lucifuge has members that look like their parents are demons, but in reality, they're descended from powerful (Rank 4+) spirits that have sired children with human partners. In certain settings, some of these Lucies are even the children of underworld gods.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:30:42-07:00","id":132398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=132340#post132340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reader should have <i>some</i> trouble telling them apart, because they are getting the experience of the characters they'll be playing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree.<br /> <br /> Firstly I don't think that the Response chapters were ever about the experience of the characters; that was found in chapter one of the first five books. Nor do I think it is a good idea to try. I found it frustrating to read. I do not think frustration is what a hunter will feel when they're trying to figure out what kind of monster they're up against. Maybe terror and desperation. A good horror fiction might be able to convey terror and desperation, but a rulebook never could. So you might as well present advice for running these organisations in a clear and useful way than fail to convey an emotion.<br /> <br /> And I don't even think divorcing people from their lore is even a good idea, because this section isn't just for players. It's for Storytellers too. The Unchained and Inferno books are packed full of themes, ideas, mechanics, advice for how to portray demons; that are useful for a Hunter storyteller. You don't want to make it harder to use that stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=132340#post132340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDITTED IN PS: By the way, one of the cool things about the Lucifuge is that their lineages are all fucked up-it's actually harder to tell who their parents are than you'd think. Inferno demons claim a large portion of it, but things like Fae-blooded folks also have room in there, and <i>certainly </i> children of the Unchained have room in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well naturally. Once you go back seven generations you have over a hundred ancestors. But their powers come from their Infernal ancestors.<br /> <br /> We have mechanics for ghoul families, fetch-spawn, wolf-blooded, etc. It's quite easy to tell the Lucifuge apart from a wolf-blooded. It's also better if you stick to just Infernal demons as the &quot;ancestor who matters&quot; because it gives a stronger central theme. The Lucifuge are defined not just by having supernatural parents, but by the nature of their parents. Inferno influences the mechanics of their Endowment, their self image, just about everything.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to loose a strong central theme, at least not without a pretty amazing replacement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-11-2014, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T13:41:31-07:00","id":132754,"title":"","content":"If you don't think a hunter will feel frustration, you are clearly playing a different game. And it's not making it harder, it's making it easier, it's changing your perspective. It's not like you lose the knowledge, you just understand better how it looks from the outside perspective. You now have been severed from actively seeing things one way, but you still know how it is, a balance between subjective experience and objective reality.<br /> <br /> Consider Mister White and Mister Blue, introduced at least a year(and more, in the case of Blue) before Inferno came out and six years before Descent. They were presented as, well, Demons. Plain ol' demons, no mention of Supernal, Abyssal, Goetic, Infernal, Unchained, Fae, Spiritual, etc. When Inferno rolled around, it's a fair bet(I wasn't there) that they were classed as infernal demons. Sometime after I came back, Rose revealed her intent of those guys as God Machine, and now you can hardly see them as anything but Unchained because that's what they are...But the hunters(and the players) of) the early Vigil days didn't know.<br /> <br /> Balance the two. You now know that Infernal and Unchained look alike. to hunters. You may know the difference, but now you also clearly know what the people who don't know everything sees.<br /> <br /> And no, I meant that the blood that gets you into the Lucifuge can be any variety of things. There's a reason there's some question as to who the Lucifuge is, there's a reason some castigations are more potent against the Fae and some against the Unchained. Blanket stating that it's all Infernal <i>kills the mystery.</i><br /> <br /> And mystery is the theme of the <i>entire World of Darkness</i>.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that in the discussion of the demons, demons as presented in Hunter are also their own catergory-they don't neatly adhere to Inferno or Descent, not without work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T15:40:33-07:00","id":132825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=132754#post132754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that in the discussion of the demons, demons as presented in Hunter are also their own catergory-they don't neatly adhere to Inferno or Descent, not without work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Both Demon: the Descent and World of Darkness: Inferno were used as inspiration and references for Hunter: Mortal Remains, but neither Rose as this chapter's writer nor David and I as developers were bound by those books. Mortal Remains is a Hunter: the Vigil supplement so it was built with Hunter games in mind. Hunters don't have copies of Demon: the Descent laying around were they can point and say this Demon is XYZ and that one is ABC from some other book...demons are demons and even different groups of Hunters will argue about what kind they are, what powers they have, and ways to fight them.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T10:34:55-07:00","id":134040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=132754#post132754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't think a hunter will feel frustration, you are clearly playing a different game.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that any frustration a hunter feels will be completely overshadowed by bone deep feelings of dread, that lives are depending on you figuring this out and quickly. The mild annoyance I feel when reading a rule book just doesn't compare to life or death situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/123404-in-which-i-read-mortal-remains?p=132754#post132754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, I meant that the blood that gets you into the Lucifuge can be any variety of things. There's a reason there's some question as to who the Lucifuge is, there's a reason some castigations are more potent against the Fae and some against the Unchained. Blanket stating that it's all Infernal <i>kills the mystery.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> And I'm actually fine with that.<br /> <br /> Hunter has twelve organisations in the core and another 18 in supplements. With 30 different groups there is room for diversity, so I would prioritise the core theme of an individual Compact or Conspiracy above the game's general themes. In the Lucifuge's case, that's the personal horror that comes from evil being quite literally a part of your genetics, and the heroism of overcoming it. That's a great theme. I'm more than happy to sacrafice some mystery about the Lucifuge's parents to preserve it because, firstly the Conspiracy itself, the Lady's motives, that's a far better mystery than &quot;demon or spirit&quot;. And secondly, because if I wanted more mystery I could always play the AKD or Canites instead.<br /> <br /> As for your point about Castigation. Lucifer was one of the highest Archangels, divine power is infinitely broad in it's uses. It seems perfectly fitting that his descendants would have diverse abilities - but the core Castigation rules are themed on biblical demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}